  "details": "Currently, only the last used instance name is remembered and set as the default.  \n\nHowever, when we give an instance a special name—for example, to celebrate someone’s birthday—we usually don’t want to reuse that name.  Such events don't repeat.\n\nOn the other hand, there are cases where we *do* want to reuse certain names, such as for recurring events like weekly meetings or “class names” for academy-style events. Still, even in those cases, we may create instances for other use cases in between repeated instances.\n\nTo address both scenarios, I suggest remembering several recent instance names and letting users choose from them when creating a new instance—similar to how status presets work. This could serve as an alternative to, or complement for, the current “reuse the last name” behavior.  \n\nRelated Canny: Default instance name should be random: https://feedback.vrchat.com/open-beta/p/1708-the-default-initial-instance-name-should-be-random-number\n\n*Note: Academy-style events (“学園型イベント” or “学園型コミュニティ” in Japanese) are a popular type of event in Japan, such as 私立VRC学園 (@VRC_HighSchool),VRCスクール (@vrcs_info), 魔術学舎 United (@UniMagicVRC).*",
